   "driver": "v4 hits $31,000-$33,000 at 300 units, 360 robots are delivered for the April 2027 season, at least 250 sell at the $16,500 list, harvest-level recovery is above 85%, and the Calder licence clears its 100-robot test on 2027-12-31.",
   "evidence": "64 robots and 75 paid seasons already delivered; 110 contracted and 50 LOIs for 2027; $4.0M of the round committed; Tallis has quoted the v4 BOM (S53, unverified). Deere paid $250M-$305M for pre-scale autonomy businesses (S96, S92).",
   "outcome": "$8M+ of ARR exiting 2027, an OEM partnership or Series B in 2028, and a trade sale at $300M-$400M in 2030-2031; Meridian returns 3.3x-4.4x after 20% Series B dilution ($40M-$53M on $12M).",
   "implication": "Invest at the current price only with a tranche that captures this case; at $72M the bull case is what the price already assumes."
  },
  {
   "case": "Base",
   "probability": "45%",
   "driver": "The build lands late or short: 180-250 robots at the $12,700 renewal, $2-3M of RaaS in 2027, a flat or slightly down Series B in 2028 once the 1x preference stack is visible, and an OEM trade sale at $150M-$250M in 2029-2031.",
   "evidence": "2027 is 44% covered (110 contracted plus 50 LOIs of 360); renewal price is below the $13,350 break-even at current service cost; the $18M funds one season and leaves $1.5-3.5M at end-2027 (S53, derived). The category base rate is failure or absorption (S114, S115, S91).",
   "outcome": "$150M-$250M sale in 2029-2031; Meridian returns 1.7x-2.8x, or 1.3x-2.2x after a 20% Series B dilution. On a $48M-$55M entry the same exit returns 2.2x-3.7x.",
   "implication": "Reprice the entry to $48M-$55M or tranche; the base case is a modest venture return at $72M, not a loss."
  },
